Quick draft SDK snippet and notes below. I'll put a short code sample in the shared folder and update the pilot checklist.

JS SDK quickstart (server-side) — auth + routing + constrained decoding (pseudo):

const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_SANDBOX_KEY, env: 'pilot-us' });

// token refresh middleware will rotate short-lived tokens using KMS-backed service key
client.on('token_expire', async () => {
  // call internal token rotation endpoint — handled by Redwood infra
});
// request tagging controls routing policy: route=quote/high_accuracy or route=search/cost_opt
const resp = await client.generate({
  model: 'redwood-rlhf-iv-1',
  route: 'quote/high_accuracy',
  prompt: buildPrompt(data),
  constraints: { // constrained decoding hints
    allowed_keys: ['carrier_id','est_days','price_cents','currency'],
    key_token_whitelist: true
  },
  function_call: 'quote_response_v1' // if available, triggers structured function-like output
});
Notes / approach
- Prefer function-calling when the model supports it — yields more deterministic key ordering and types.
- If function-calling not available for a variant, use constrained decoding + post-validate.
- For reranker: call embeddings API then reranker endpoint; tag final request with route=quote/high_accuracy to ensure the right model and KV-cache warm path.

I'll drop the code file into the shared Drive and annotate the key rotation step for Clement.

—Marissa
